== 2. Source: the locks the new readings take ==
- holds (session.go:360), on a "lost" reading, takes the sessions' lock (settledMark). It is
  called from wait.Run's Alive, at the top of each tick (internal/wait/wait.go:159), outside
  the record's lock. The listener holds its role's presence lock then: presence, then
  sessions, the same order as everywhere.
- fyi, away and back read who has each role inside AppendAll, under the record's lock.
  That reading is the session files and wait.Listening, which tries the presence lock with
  LOCK_NB (internal/wait/presence.go:96), so it never waits there.
- tryMoveContinued answers "ambiguous" only at session.go:705, under lockRoles.

